  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender, Rights and Opportunities for Women - Through Fungi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GROW2025 was a two day workshop during The International Fungal Conservation Conference
November 4-5, 2025 Cotonou, Benin. It included participants from Benin, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Malawi and Tanzania. GROW2025 brought together researchers and practitioners working at a range of career stages on topics including fungal resource use, ethnomycology, gender equality, public health, women&#x2019;s reproductive health care, and development issues. For more see africanfungivoices.org</narrative>
  </description>
